source: OpenCode v2.3.2 question tool (2.1.2). Real: the pane chrome (2-column inset, ┃ border, sidebar at column 94), copied from permission-shell-2.3.2.txt, which was measured from a real read of a 2.3.2 pane. Reconstructed from the 2.3.2 binary's own form code (/home/bill/.opencode/bin/opencode, the "question" tool and its form dialog): the form title "Questions", the field description (the question), "N. label" option rows with descriptions three columns further in, the automatic "Type your own answer" row, the footer "↑↓ select  enter submit  esc dismiss", and the paddings and gaps between them. Not a live capture of a question dialog. Neutral demo content only; herdr reports OpenCode panes as done or idle, hence blocked false.
